models/tec/malthus.py: schedules of models/res/coupled.py; r* = 12000; g' = 0.050; kappa = 0.060 a year

== A. a pure quota (RES 8.2 regime A, eta = 1): N* = N_bind * RMAX * T / r*, the population tracks a moving N*
   r* = 12000, RMAX = 20000, g' = 0.050, kappa = r* g' / 10 000 = 0.060 a year (time constant 16.7 years)
   A1. a trend of TrendBP of gain a year, from the fixed point N*(T = 1) = 100 000, no cap in the window
       predicted premium (the ratio above r* once the population tracks): TrendBP * 10 000 / (10 000 + G) / g'  bp
       TrendBP  year      G    N/N*   ratio  premium predicted
            25    20    500   0.972   12348      348       476
            25    40   1000   0.965   12437      437       455
            25    60   1500   0.964   12444      444       435
            50    20   1000   0.946   12677      677       909
            50    40   2000   0.936   12818      818       833
            50    60   3000   0.937   12809      809       769
           100    20   2000   0.902   13297     1297      1667
           100    40   4000   0.891   13465     1465      1429
           100    60   6000   0.898   13362     1362      1250
   A2. a one-off step of +1 000 bp (a discovery), from N*(T = 1): the ratio jumps, the population follows, e-fold time 1 / kappa
       N*(T = 1.1) = 110000; ratio at year 0: 13200, 5: 12869, 10: 12634, 20: 12344, 40: 12108, 80: 12019
       the gap N*' - N falls to 1/e of its start at year 17 (the linearisation: 16.7); N at year 120 is 109809 of 110000
   A3. the trend reaches its cap (CapBP 1 000 at TrendBP 50: year 20): the premium is paid back, with no overshoot
       year:     10     20     30     40     60     80    120
       ratio: 12448  12677  12368  12203  12067  12027  12019
       N/N*' at year 120: 0.998; the largest N/N*' over the run: 0.998 (no overshoot of the new fixed point: monotone)
   A4. eta: with a curve through the origin the elasticity of the ratio to N is below 1 and the premium is larger (1 / eta)
       see part C (a stock): the same step, a refilling stock with a linear abundance curve

== B. a refilling stock with a linear abundance curve (RES 8.2 regime B): the stock share falls with T
   sigma*(T) = r* / (RMAX T) = 0.6 / T; N*(T) = R C (1 - sigma*) / (h TPY); a(sigma*) = 10 000 r* / (r_full)
       T sigma* pred   N* pred  N at 400y  ratio sigma sim min N/N*0
    1.00       0.600    100000     100000  12010     0.601     1.000
    1.10       0.545    113636     113578  12018     0.546     1.000
    1.20       0.500    125000     124971  12016     0.501     1.000
    1.50       0.400    150000     150061  12015     0.401     1.000
   (the rate 0.5 a year is above the monotone threshold 0.16, so the approach is monotone for every T tried; the threshold 4 kappa (1 - sigma) / sigma rises as sigma* falls:)
   T 1.00: sigma* 0.600, monotone iff R >= 0.160 a year
   T 1.20: sigma* 0.500, monotone iff R >= 0.240 a year
   T 1.50: sigma* 0.400, monotone iff R >= 0.360 a year
   T 2.00: sigma* 0.300, monotone iff R >= 0.560 a year

== C. a logistic stock: a gain moves sigma* toward the maximum-yield point 0.5; below it the fixed point is a saddle
   sigma*(T) = 0.6 / T, so T_crit = 1.2: a gain of +20% at the start is the edge (the plan share 6 000, a linear curve):
   the validator's inequality  a(5 000) * (10 000 + CapBP) >= a(sigma_plan) * 10 000  gives CapBP >= 2 000 here
       T  sigma*  N*/N*0 min N/N*0 max N/N*0 stock/cap 300y  outcome
    1.00   0.600   1.000     1.000     1.000          0.601  monotone
    1.05   0.571   1.020     1.000     1.026          0.572  damped oscillation (undershoot 2.0% of N*)
    1.10   0.545   1.033     1.000     1.049          0.546  damped oscillation (undershoot 3.2% of N*)
    1.15   0.522   1.040     1.000     1.070          0.523  damped oscillation (undershoot 3.8% of N*)
    1.18   0.508   1.041     0.982     1.082          0.517  small residual
    1.20   0.500   1.042     0.881     1.099          0.399  sustained cycle
    1.25   0.480   1.040     0.004     1.109          0.000  collapse
    1.40   0.429   1.020     0.004     1.159          0.000  collapse
   a ramp that crosses it: TrendBP of gain a year from T = 1, no cap, from the fixed point; the stock is exhausted when it falls below 2% of its capacity:
   TrendBP  crossing  N/N*0 at it   exhausted  years after  ratio at 10y before
